    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a clear focus on maximizing run production against a series of mid-to-high xERA matchups. The centerpiece of our offense is **Gunnar Henderson**, who leads the team with a strong 80.76 score. Facing McGreevy, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a massive 14% boost due to dynamic platoon advantages and a favorable batting order spot, making him our highest-ceiling asset. He is closely followed by **Kyle Tucker** (77.97) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (77.71). **Kyle Tucker** enjoys the day\u2019s best matchup against the 5.23 xERA of Smith-Shawver, while **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** capitalizes on a high-leverage opportunity against Dobnak, whose 4.79 xERA underscores a prime environment for run creation. Additionally, **Jackson Merrill** (75.10) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.41) round out a core group that we expect to drive the bulk of our 5x5 production today.\n\nStrategic benching remains vital for preserving our game caps, particularly with **Heliot Ramos** unavailable due to a confirmed benching. The most difficult personnel decision involved **Luis Lara** (51.97), who narrowly missed the starting cut in favor of **Tommy White** (55.97). While **Luis Lara** carries the upside of an elite SP skill boost, **Tommy White**\u2019s favorable platoon outlook against the left-handed Prielipp and a +10% park factor ultimately secured him the UTIL slot. Meanwhile, we continue to monitor the status of our injured core, including **Andy Pages**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Jacob Wilson**, as their absence remains a significant drag on our depth. We are also keeping a watchful eye on **Nasim Nunez** (56.21); while his power profile is limited, his specific utility in the stolen base category\u2014leveraged by an opportunistic matchup against a slow-delivering pitcher\u2014is exactly the type of \"efficiency play\" the Austin Waves prioritize to gain ground in the scarcest scoring category.",
